Subject: [PATCH] inputflinger: strength of the vibration of the controllers

persist.sys.pocketds.rumble (percent, 0 to 100, set by the PocketDS Extra overlay) scales both
rumble magnitudes in EventHub::vibrate, where every vibration of an input device goes (games
through InputDevice.getVibratorManager, and the system effects of base 0007). Unset, out of
range or 100: nothing changes.

diff --git a/services/inputflinger/reader/EventHub.cpp b/services/inputflinger/reader/EventHub.cpp
--- a/services/inputflinger/reader/EventHub.cpp
+++ b/services/inputflinger/reader/EventHub.cpp
@@ -1820,6 +1820,16 @@
         // evdev FF_RUMBLE effect only supports two channels of vibration.
         effect.u.rumble.strong_magnitude = element.getMagnitude(FF_STRONG_MAGNITUDE_CHANNEL_IDX);
         effect.u.rumble.weak_magnitude = element.getMagnitude(FF_WEAK_MAGNITUDE_CHANNEL_IDX);
+        // Ayaneo Pocket DS: strength of the vibration of the controllers, chosen in PocketDS
+        // Extra (persist.sys.pocketds.rumble, percent, 0 to 100). Every vibration of a
+        // controller goes through here (games and the system). Unset or 100: unchanged.
+        const int32_t rumble = property_get_int32("persist.sys.pocketds.rumble", 100);
+        if (rumble >= 0 && rumble < 100) {
+            effect.u.rumble.strong_magnitude =
+                    static_cast<uint16_t>(effect.u.rumble.strong_magnitude * rumble / 100);
+            effect.u.rumble.weak_magnitude =
+                    static_cast<uint16_t>(effect.u.rumble.weak_magnitude * rumble / 100);
+        }
         effect.replay.length = element.duration.count();
         effect.replay.delay = 0;
         if (ioctl(device->fd, EVIOCSFF, &effect)) {
